# Feedback Fixer

## When to Use
When you receive batch app-build feedback or error reports and need to systematically fix the agent pack. Invoke by providing feedback, e.g.: "feedback: QVAC model loading fails with timeout on first run".

## Workflow

### 1. Parse and Triage
- Extract each issue as a concrete task
- Identify affected modules/recipes/core docs
- Mark severity: **blocking** (app won't build) vs **improvement** (works but confusing)

### 2. Verify Against Sources
- Prefer local source code and reference apps
- Cross-check with battle-tested apps:
  - `sandbox/coffee-assistant/` (AI + P2P + RPC reference)
  - `sandbox/coffee-assistant-ui/` (Pear Desktop + worker pattern)
  - `sandbox/slack-p2p-copy/` (P2P messaging)
  - `reference-apps/qvac-workbench-desktop/` (upstream Pear Desktop)
  - `reference-apps/qvac-workbench-mobile/` (upstream Expo Bare)
  - `reference-apps/qvac-health/` (upstream mobile health)
- If info is missing, add a `> **Note**:` in docs

### 3. Update Agent Pack
- Edit files directly in `packages/agent-pack/src/`
- Follow templates from research-writing-guide rule
- Update code snippets to match actual signatures
- Add troubleshooting entries for repeated failures

### 4. Sync to CLI
```bash
cp -r packages/agent-pack/src/* packages/cli/agent-pack-src/
```

## Rules
- Edit `packages/agent-pack/src/` directly — all content lives there
- Do NOT invent APIs — only use verified types from source
- If a breaking change is reported, search for ALL dependent snippets and fix consistently

## Triage Template
```markdown
| # | Issue | Severity | Module | File to Fix |
|---|-------|----------|--------|-------------|
| 1 | [summary] | blocking/improvement | [module] | [path] |
```
